1
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,253
JESUS: A new commandment I give you.

2
00:00:06,603 --> 00:00:08,465
JESUS: My command is this:

3
00:00:08,665 --> 00:00:12,044
JESUS: Love one another... as I have loved you.

4
00:00:12,994 --> 00:00:16,323
He said this on the night He was betrayed...

5
00:00:16,423 --> 00:00:22,019
only moments after handing bread to Judas, the man who would betray Him.

6
00:00:26,769 --> 00:00:31,936
Behind this door, an old man waits to die... for the name of Jesus.

7
00:00:32,186 --> 00:00:39,916
His name is Paul. Long ago, this same man persecuted Jesus... by hunting down those who followed Him.

8
00:00:40,966 --> 00:00:44,124
The man standing outside is Asher.

9
00:00:44,174 --> 00:00:47,503
When he was a boy, Paul took his father from him...

10
00:00:47,553 --> 00:00:50,708
and Asher has hated him ever since.

11
00:00:51,157 --> 00:00:53,059
ASHER: Bread. I'm bringing him bread.

12
00:00:53,609 --> 00:00:55,395
ASHER: I don't even want to be here.

13
00:00:55,745 --> 00:00:58,217
ASHER: Why am I even here? This is foolish.

14
00:01:00,367 --> 00:01:04,805
Months earlier, in a house where followers of Jesus gathered...

15
00:01:04,855 --> 00:01:08,520
a letter from the apostle Paul was read aloud.

16
00:01:08,770 --> 00:01:13,510
PHOEBE: Paul, a servant of Christ Jesus... to all in Rome who are loved by God.

17
00:01:14,560 --> 00:01:17,144
PHOEBE: Do not repay anyone evil for evil.

18
00:01:17,394 --> 00:01:21,931
PHOEBE: If it is possible, as far as it depends on you... live at peace with everyone.

19
00:01:22,181 --> 00:01:27,179
PHOEBE: If your enemy is hungry, feed him. If he is thirsty, give him something to drink.

20
00:01:27,329 --> 00:01:30,571
PHOEBE: In doing this, you will heap burning coals on his head.

21
00:01:33,121 --> 00:01:34,421
ASHER: His own words.

22
00:01:35,072 --> 00:01:36,757
ASHER: Let's see if he believes them.

23
00:01:39,707 --> 00:01:41,602
GUARD: Food for the old man?

24
00:01:41,852 --> 00:01:45,007
GUARD: You're the first one in a week. Make it quick.

25
00:01:47,457 --> 00:01:49,999
PAUL: My brother Luke... is that you?

26
00:01:50,349 --> 00:01:53,254
PAUL: Come in, come in! Thank you for seeing me.

27
00:01:53,404 --> 00:01:59,322
PAUL: The Lord provides... He blesses us in ways we sometimes can't possibly imagine.

28
00:01:59,572 --> 00:02:02,613
PAUL: And you've brought bread. God bless us all.

29
00:02:02,863 --> 00:02:06,629
PAUL: So many are afraid to come now. I don't blame them.

30
00:02:06,778 --> 00:02:08,208
PAUL: But you came.

31
00:02:09,458 --> 00:02:10,584
ASHER: I'm not Luke.

32
00:02:11,034 --> 00:02:15,534
ASHER: But... thank you. For thinking I could be someone so dear to you.

33
00:02:16,184 --> 00:02:18,390
PAUL: Then who are you, my friend?

34
00:02:18,940 --> 00:02:23,134
ASHER: Someone you met once... in Jerusalem. A long time ago.

35
00:02:23,384 --> 00:02:26,629
ASHER: The street of the potters. A house with a blue door.

36
00:02:26,979 --> 00:02:29,925
ASHER: You came at night... with the temple guard.

37
00:02:30,575 --> 00:02:33,286
ASHER: You dragged a man named Yosef into the street.

38
00:02:33,436 --> 00:02:34,852
ASHER: In front of his wife.

39
00:02:34,902 --> 00:02:36,317
ASHER: In front of his son.

40
00:02:37,067 --> 00:02:38,592
PAUL: Yosef...

41
00:02:39,442 --> 00:02:43,973
ASHER: I was eight years old. I watched it all... through a crack in the door.

42
00:02:44,623 --> 00:02:46,275
ASHER: He never came home.

43
00:02:49,226 --> 00:02:50,834
PAUL: He looked at me.

44
00:02:51,385 --> 00:02:54,732
PAUL: When we bound his hands... he looked straight at me.

45
00:02:54,982 --> 00:02:57,923
PAUL: Not with hatred. I knew hatred.

46
00:02:58,273 --> 00:03:02,463
PAUL: He looked at me as if... as if he was sorry for me.

47
00:03:06,313 --> 00:03:07,949
YOUNG ASHER: Father! Don't go!

48
00:03:09,499 --> 00:03:13,114
YOSEF: Asher, my son... don't be afraid for me.

49
00:03:13,364 --> 00:03:17,618
YOSEF: I am in the hands of God. He will keep me safe...

50
00:03:17,668 --> 00:03:22,727
YOSEF: and He who blesses us all will keep you safe, forever and ever.

51
00:03:23,377 --> 00:03:24,333
PAUL: Take him!

52
00:03:25,883 --> 00:03:29,273
YOSEF: May God open your eyes, my son.

53
00:03:33,023 --> 00:03:33,883
ASHER: Don't.

54
00:03:34,133 --> 00:03:35,856
ASHER: You don't get to remember him.

55
00:03:36,306 --> 00:03:38,970
PAUL: I remember him because I must.

56
00:03:39,220 --> 00:03:43,785
PAUL: Every soul I wounded is a soul the Son came to save...

57
00:03:43,835 --> 00:03:47,092
PAUL: your father... and you... and even me.

58
00:03:47,442 --> 00:03:51,723
PAUL: I will spend every breath I have left proclaiming His mercy...

59
00:03:51,773 --> 00:03:57,875
PAUL: until it reaches all of them. Even the ones lost to me... or even to time.

60
00:03:59,625 --> 00:04:01,627
ASHER: They read your letter to us in Rome.

61
00:04:01,877 --> 00:04:04,533
ASHER: “If your enemy is hungry, feed him.”

62
00:04:04,883 --> 00:04:06,420
ASHER: So. I'm feeding you.

63
00:04:08,570 --> 00:04:11,701
PAUL: Then you have done what I only wrote about.

64
00:04:11,951 --> 00:04:16,770
PAUL: You are fulfilling the word of the Son... by helping a sheep like me.

65
00:04:17,120 --> 00:04:19,250
ASHER: Spare me. Don't make me a saint.

66
00:04:19,500 --> 00:04:21,232
ASHER: You act like a saint now...

67
00:04:21,252 --> 00:04:24,913
ASHER: but you weren't acting like a saint when you destroyed my life.

68
00:04:25,163 --> 00:04:27,639
ASHER: Do your followers even know what you were?

69
00:04:28,089 --> 00:04:29,193
PAUL: They know.

70
00:04:29,343 --> 00:04:33,130
PAUL: I put it in my letters, so that no one forgets.

71
00:04:33,481 --> 00:04:38,829
PAUL: I was a blasphemer... and a persecutor... and a violent man.

72
00:04:39,379 --> 00:04:41,981
PAUL: I thought I was defending God.

73
00:04:42,331 --> 00:04:44,102
PAUL: I was hunting Him.

74
00:04:44,852 --> 00:04:49,981
PAUL: I carried the pain of what I did with me... all the way to Damascus.

75
00:04:50,231 --> 00:04:52,948
PAUL: I had orders to arrest more of them.

76
00:04:56,898 --> 00:05:00,474
JESUS: Paul... Paul. Why do you persecute me?

77
00:05:00,924 --> 00:05:02,541
PAUL: Who are you, Lord?

78
00:05:03,091 --> 00:05:07,940
JESUS: I am Jesus. I came to save those who are not yet saved.

79
00:05:08,890 --> 00:05:11,241
JESUS: You are precious to me, Paul.

80
00:05:11,391 --> 00:05:17,467
JESUS: Open your heart to me... and carry the Holy Spirit, with me and my Father.

81
00:05:18,017 --> 00:05:21,659
PAUL: I had a sense that my destruction was deserved...

82
00:05:21,909 --> 00:05:25,793
PAUL: and yet He looked at me... the same way Yosef had.

83
00:05:26,243 --> 00:05:31,227
PAUL: I was shown mercy, because I acted in ignorance and unbelief.

84
00:05:31,377 --> 00:05:35,362
PAUL: The grace of our Lord was poured out on me abundantly...

85
00:05:35,382 --> 00:05:39,763
PAUL: along with the faith and love that are in Christ Jesus.

86
00:05:40,113 --> 00:05:44,403
PAUL: I thank Christ Jesus our Lord, who has given me strength...

87
00:05:44,453 --> 00:05:48,972
PAUL: that He considered me trustworthy, appointing me to His service.

88
00:05:49,322 --> 00:05:54,736
PAUL: He chose me... the very one who hunted those in partnership with Him.

89
00:05:55,486 --> 00:05:56,661
ASHER: So that's it?

90
00:05:56,911 --> 00:05:59,796
ASHER: You saw a light... and all your sin washed away?

91
00:06:00,146 --> 00:06:03,434
ASHER: And my father was just... the price of converting?

92
00:06:04,084 --> 00:06:05,100
PAUL: No.

93
00:06:05,450 --> 00:06:09,958
PAUL: Nothing washes away the memory of your father. Not for me.

94
00:06:10,308 --> 00:06:14,881
PAUL: I see his face every time I write the word “mercy.”

95
00:06:16,131 --> 00:06:20,740
PAUL: Here is a trustworthy saying that deserves full acceptance:

96
00:06:20,890 --> 00:06:24,778
PAUL: Christ Jesus came into the world to save sinners...

97
00:06:25,028 --> 00:06:27,505
PAUL: of whom I am the worst.

98
00:06:28,155 --> 00:06:31,495
PAUL: But for that very reason, I was shown mercy...

99
00:06:31,545 --> 00:06:35,949
PAUL: by Him, the Lord... the One who saved me from myself...

100
00:06:36,099 --> 00:06:42,349
PAUL: so that in me, the worst of sinners, Christ Jesus might display His immense patience...

101
00:06:42,399 --> 00:06:47,985
PAUL: as an example for those who would believe in Him... and receive eternal life.

102
00:06:48,735 --> 00:06:50,375
ASHER: I came here to hate you.

103
00:06:50,925 --> 00:06:52,950
ASHER: I rehearsed it. For years.

104
00:06:53,300 --> 00:06:55,576
ASHER: You say all these beautiful things...

105
00:06:55,726 --> 00:07:00,116
ASHER: but I don't think I will ever love you... like you seem to want me to.

106
00:07:00,766 --> 00:07:01,875
PAUL: I know.

107
00:07:02,225 --> 00:07:04,476
PAUL: And I will not hate you back.

108
00:07:04,726 --> 00:07:07,235
PAUL: And I will respect your boundary.

109
00:07:07,385 --> 00:07:12,995
PAUL: Love is only something that can be grown... never forced, or coerced...

110
00:07:13,045 --> 00:07:16,238
PAUL: not even by God, blessed be His name.

111
00:07:16,589 --> 00:07:19,511
PAUL: The hate you give me is from God.

112
00:07:20,061 --> 00:07:24,330
PAUL: The prayers I pray will be not just for you, but for the world...

113
00:07:24,380 --> 00:07:28,088
PAUL: in His mighty name, every day that I have left.

114
00:07:28,338 --> 00:07:32,325
PAUL: And I will see you as a brother, as long as I live.

115
00:07:32,875 --> 00:07:33,836
ASHER: Look...

116
00:07:34,486 --> 00:07:35,924
ASHER: I am not your brother.

117
00:07:36,574 --> 00:07:39,533
PAUL: You are right. I am no brother to you.

118
00:07:41,483 --> 00:07:44,850
PAUL: But the Lord is patient. He sat with me.

119
00:07:45,400 --> 00:07:46,558
ASHER: And still...

120
00:07:46,909 --> 00:07:48,295
ASHER: I brought the bread.

121
00:07:49,045 --> 00:07:54,623
JESUS: A new commandment I give you: love one another, as I have loved you.

122
00:08:01,573 --> 00:08:03,548
ASHER: I don't forgive you. Not yet.

123
00:08:04,098 --> 00:08:06,802
ASHER: But my father would have shared his bread with you...

124
00:08:06,952 --> 00:08:08,178
ASHER: so I will.

125
00:08:11,228 --> 00:08:14,128
PAUL: Burning coals... on my head.

126
00:08:14,678 --> 00:08:16,664
PAUL: I wrote those words...

127
00:08:16,814 --> 00:08:22,406
PAUL: I never knew how much the love of Christ would burn me... but for the better.

128
00:08:23,156 --> 00:08:25,860
Do not be overcome by evil...

129
00:08:26,110 --> 00:08:28,783
but overcome evil with good.

130
00:08:30,733 --> 00:08:31,990
GUARD: Time's up.

131
00:08:32,340 --> 00:08:36,373
GUARD: And you, old man... your execution is tomorrow. At first light.

132
00:08:37,323 --> 00:08:38,402
ASHER: Tomorrow?

133
00:08:38,852 --> 00:08:40,479
PAUL: I understand.

134
00:08:40,729 --> 00:08:42,375
GUARD: Say your goodbyes.

135
00:08:43,324 --> 00:08:44,628
ASHER: Aren't you afraid?

136
00:08:45,578 --> 00:08:47,848
PAUL: The Lord provides, Asher.

137
00:08:48,198 --> 00:08:51,493
PAUL: Who shall separate us from the love of Christ?

138
00:08:51,743 --> 00:08:55,243
PAUL: Shall trouble, or hardship, or persecution...

139
00:08:55,263 --> 00:08:59,097
PAUL: or famine, or nakedness, or danger, or sword?

140
00:08:59,347 --> 00:09:03,722
PAUL: As it is written: “For your sake we face death all day long;

141
00:09:03,742 --> 00:09:07,008
PAUL: we are considered as sheep to be slaughtered.”

142
00:09:07,358 --> 00:09:11,794
PAUL: No! In all these things we are more than simple conquerors...

143
00:09:11,814 --> 00:09:14,194
PAUL: through Him who loved us.

144
00:09:14,544 --> 00:09:17,983
PAUL: For I am convinced that neither death nor life,

145
00:09:18,003 --> 00:09:23,753
PAUL: neither angels nor demons, neither the present nor the future, nor any powers,

146
00:09:23,773 --> 00:09:28,221
PAUL: neither height nor depth, nor anything else in all creation...

147
00:09:28,271 --> 00:09:33,048
PAUL: will be able to separate us from the love of the Lord our God...

148
00:09:33,068 --> 00:09:39,589
PAUL: that is in Christ Jesus... the One sent from heaven to save us from ourselves.

149
00:09:40,139 --> 00:09:41,286
ASHER: Thank you.

150
00:09:43,236 --> 00:09:46,585
At first light, the old man was no more.

151
00:09:47,235 --> 00:09:53,778
Among the few who were present with him to the end... was the one who had every reason to hate him.

152
00:09:55,727 --> 00:09:58,639
ASHER: Lord... I don't know how to love him yet.

153
00:09:59,088 --> 00:10:00,326
ASHER: Teach me.

154
00:10:02,476 --> 00:10:07,058
JESUS: Learn from me... for I am gentle and humble in heart.

155
00:10:09,808 --> 00:10:12,335
JESUS: A new commandment I give you.

156
00:10:12,684 --> 00:10:14,753
JESUS: My command is this:

157
00:10:15,003 --> 00:10:18,656
JESUS: love one another... as I have loved you.

